I come out of the grocery store.
Then I go to the nearby vegetable cart.
There are plenty of fresh vegetables there.
There is a vegetable vendor at the cart.
I say to him, "Dada, give me some onions."
He asks, "Madam, how many onions should I give?"
I tell him, "Give a quarter kilo of onions."
"And also give some fresh green chilies."
He puts the onions and chilies in a bag.
After that, I myself take one big lemon.
I ask, "Dada, do you have fresh coriander?"
He says yes and gives me a big bunch of coriander.
I now have all the vegetables from my list.
I ask, "How much money is it?"
He says, "Madam, it is forty-five rupees."
I give him fifty rupees.
He gives me five rupees back.
I take the bag of vegetables and start walking towards home.
